description: "Separate spectral-line emission from continuum in ALMA data: pick line-free channels, fit and subtract the continuum in the uv plane (uvcontsub) or image plane (imcontsub, STATCONT), and build the matching continuum image from the same channels. Use when making line cubes, moment maps, line fluxes or continuum images from ALMA spectral data, when a field is line-rich (hot cores, starbursts, spectral scans), when lines sit in absorption against bright continuum, or when a referee asks how the continuum was removed. Built from 656 ALMA papers (2012-2026)."
---

# Continuum subtraction and line-free channel selection

Continuum subtraction fits a low-order model of the continuum across channels that carry no line emission and
removes it, leaving a line-only cube; the same line-free channels give the continuum image. Two mistakes matter
most: (1) a wrong line-free channel set (line wings, blends or absorption inside the "continuum" channels) biases
both the line flux and the continuum flux, and (2) papers almost never report which channels they used, so the
result cannot be reproduced. Over 200 cards in the pack flag the line-free channel ranges as not stated (sum of
the variant labels in the pack's "not stated" list).

Counts below marked "pack aggregate" come from the pack's aggregate sections. Counts marked "my count" come from
my own count of the pack's per-paper parameter lines, which list 486 of the 656 papers; I left out papers that are
clearly off-topic for this technique.

## When to use

- Any ALMA line cube, moment map or line flux where the source has detectable continuum (dust, free-free,
  synchrotron, a quasar core, a planet or comet body).
- Building a continuum image from the same spectral windows that carry lines (flag or exclude line channels,
  then MFS/mtmfs image the rest) (2024ApJ...972..111L, 2018MNRAS.475..448T, 2021A&A...648A..19W).
- Line-rich sources where few channels are line-free: hot cores, complex organics, starburst nuclei, spectral
  scans. Here the statistical image-plane methods (STATCONT) are used instead of a hand-picked channel list
  (2020A&A...636A..67A, 2021A&A...656A..46M, 2018ApJ...866...87B).
- Line searches at high redshift where the line falls in one spw and the other spws give the continuum
  (2013ApJ...770...13W, 2019ApJ...873...50D, 2020A&A...636A..37D).

## When not to use

- **Absorption against a bright continuum.** You may need the continuum kept. Papers fitted absorption on
  non-subtracted spectra with an explicit continuum background layer (2018A&A...615A.141B, XCLASS with
  T_B = 132 K background), or subtracted in the image plane because uv-plane subtraction "can cause artifacts in
  the presence of absorption features" (2015ApJ...814...22E). Optical depth needs the continuum level, so measure
  and keep it.
- **Not enough line-free channels to define the continuum.** Some papers skipped subtraction for that window
  (2014ApJ...790..160S, CO(3-2)) or fitted continuum as a free constant together with the line (Gaussian plus
  constant: 2013ApJ...770...13W, 2026ApJ..1002L..28Y; first-order baseline fitted simultaneously with lines:
  2018A&A...620A.115B; continuum as a free parameter in a blind search on the non-subtracted cube:
  2018Natur.556..469M). Use those instead of forcing a fit through line emission.
- **Single-dish / Total Power spectra.** These use straight-line spectral baseline fits to emission-free channels
  (2018ApJ...867..166S), not uvcontsub.
- **A bright compact source that dominates the field** (quasar core, star, planet disk): subtract a source model
  from the visibilities first (uvsub of a CLEAN or fitted model), then uvcontsub the residual
  (2019MNRAS.485.1595P; 2019AJ....157..251T subtracted a limb-darkened Neptune model before deconvolution).
- **Continuum fluxes contaminated by a strong line in broadband data** (no line-free channels at all in a band):
  remove the line contribution from the continuum flux instead (2015Natur.522..455C).

## Steps

1. **Calibrate, then self-calibrate on the continuum before subtracting.** Goal: the best gains for both products.
   Method: self-calibrate on line-free channels, apply the same tables to the line data, then subtract
   (2018ApJ...852..122H, 2018A&A...615A..28D, 2021A&A...648A..19W, 2017ApJ...840...60B, 2019ApJ...871...48P).
   One paper applied a phase self-cal table after the subtraction instead (2020ApJ...898...10T). Software: CASA
   gaincal/applycal.
2. **Put all data in one velocity frame if you combine epochs or moving targets.** Doppler-correct with cvel /
   mstransform and fix phase centers before combining; for comets the order was phaseshift, uvcontsub, then cvel2
   to the comet rest frame (2025NatAs...9.1476C); uvcontsub3 was run after cvel in 2016ApJ...817..168H. Proper
   motion: fixvis/fixplanets (2018ApJ...852..122H).
3. **Find the line-free channels.** Goal: a channel set with no emission, absorption, or atmospheric features.
   Methods seen in the pack:
   - inspect amplitude vs channel in plotms and flag line peaks (2018AJ....155...47A, 2019MNRAS.483.1624B,
     2018MNRAS.475..448T);
   - exclude a fixed velocity window around each known line (table below);
   - make a first image, mark weak lines, redo (iterative): 2019Natur.570...83M required the residual slope to be
     < 30 mJy across each window, chosen within 1 arcsec of the target; 2019A&A...627A.114K iterated the
     pure-continuum ranges; 2017PASJ...69...18T picked them from an initial naturally weighted image;
   - for line-rich fields, STATCONT sigma clipping plus an aggregate deviation spectrum; line-free fraction was
     typically 10-20% of the bandwidth (2018ApJ...866...87B), followed by 2019ApJ...882..118X and
     2018ApJ...863L..35M; 2017ApJ...837L..29H reports < 5% residual line contamination with that procedure;
   - drop band edges and atmospheric lines (2017A&A...600A.141K, 2019MNRAS.488.5029H; 2019A&A...630A..59B
     excluded channels with atmospheric transmission < 0.5; 2017A&A...603A..92V stayed far from the 183 GHz water
     line).
4. **Fit and subtract the continuum.** Default in the literature: CASA uvcontsub in the uv plane with a 0th or 1st
   order polynomial over the line-free channels of the same spw (about 115 papers name uvcontsub, my count).
   Alternatives: fit the continuum spws and apply the model to the line spw (2019ApJ...873...50D,
   2019A&A...624L...7V, 2013ApJ...763..120C with a CLEAN-component model); image-plane imcontsub
   (2024ApJ...961..228S, 2019ApJ...871..170M); per-pixel STATCONT (2021A&A...656A..46M, 2017A&A...604A...6S);
   GILDAS UV_CONTINUUM + UV_SUBTRACT or UV-BASELINE (2019A&A...632A..33A, 2021A&A...652A..98G); AIPS UVLSF
   (2015ApJ...808...97Y); MIRIAD image-plane polynomials (2015ApJ...814...22E).
5. **Subtract per data set before combining** with other arrays, epochs or single-dish data (2014A&A...572L...9R,
   2019ApJ...887...88E, 2017A&A...601A...4A and 2017A&A...607L...5Q before merging with IRAM 30m;
   2020ApJ...892L..18I subtracted per cycle then combined with inverse-variance weights).
6. **Image the continuum from the same line-free channels.** MFS or mtmfs; note the effective bandwidth is smaller
   than the full band (about half in 2015ApJ...801...82H; 2902 MHz in 2018ApJ...859...35G; 5.61 GHz in
   2020ApJ...897L..33J; about 7.5 GHz in 2018PASJ...70...36I). Averaging the remaining channels to 125 MHz
   before continuum imaging was used by 2021A&A...648A..19W.
7. **Image the line cube and run the checks below.** Measure noise in line-free channels of the subtracted cube
   (2024ApJ...966...59S used 1000 random apertures in line-free channels; 2024MNRAS.527.9343L cleaned to 1.5x the
   line-free rms).

### CASA notes (general practice, not from the pack)

- Pre-6.5 `uvcontsub(vis, fitspw='0:20~110;400~480', fitorder=0|1, want_cont=False)` writes `vis.contsub`.
  CASA 6.5 and later replaced it with `uvcontsub(vis, outputvis, fitspec=..., fitorder=..., fitmethod=...)` and
  kept the old one as `uvcontsub_old`. Check `help(uvcontsub)` for the installed version before writing calls.
- `imcontsub(imagename, linefile, contfile, fitorder, chans)` fits each pixel's spectrum in an image cube; run it
  on the same cube grid and spectral frame you analyse.
- The ALMA pipeline also does continuum subtraction for its delivered cubes (pack examples: 2018A&A...617A..54L,
  2019MNRAS.489..349R, 2019MNRAS.490.5860S). Treat pipeline channel ranges as a starting point and re-check them
  for line-rich sources.

