### Assumptions (bibcode: value)
- 2018A&A...615A.141B: LTE; extended foreground filling beam
- 2018PASJ...70...36I: H0=70, OmegaM=0.3, OmegaL=0.7
- 2018A&A...615A..28D: Optically thin dust, opacity ~7 cm2/g, dust temperature 200-650 K (IK Tau) and 400-1530 K (R Dor)
- 2020A&A...636A..67A: LTE; H2CO modeled with source size ~0.15'' below beam
- 2020A&A...636A..67A: N(H2) from continuum with Tdust=100 K, kappa=1.0 cm2/g, gas-to-dust 100
- 2024ApJ...966...59S: Gas radii are lower limits due to cloud absorption and resolved-out emission
- 2020ApJ...905...85S: constant continuum across the band; alternate-sideband continuum or SED used when few line-free channels
- 2021A&A...656A..46M: Beta=1.9 emissivity law
- 2019A&A...628A.118B: intrinsic QSO continuum variation across spw0/spw1 less than 1%
- 2024MNRAS.527.9343L: R21 = 1; alpha_CO = 4.3 Msun pc-2 (K km/s)-1 including heavy elements; adopted distances
- 2016ApJ...829....6W: Flux uncertainty dominated by 10% absolute flux scale
- 2019MNRAS.485..229R: X_CO = 2e20 cm-2 (K km/s)-1; D_L = 242.4 Mpc
- 2017Icar..286..289L: Spectra represent central pointing flux; ~10% flux loss from beam convolution
- 2020A&A...644A..84M: Td = 150 K, beta = 2.0, k0 = 0.8 cm2/g at 220 GHz, mu = 2.33, gas-to-dust 100
- 2024A&A...689A.317G: Continuum constant within each spectral window (spectral index 2, <1% variation)
- 2024A&A...689A.317G: LTE; optically thin Gaussian dust; SiO abundance 6.6e-6; distance 265 pc
- 2019ApJ...871..107F: ISM isotope ratios 16O/18O=557, 12C/13C=70
- 2017MNRAS.465.2595M: Inclination 37 deg, same as outer belt
- 2016ApJ...820L..25Y: dust and gas thermally coupled with the same temperature; HCO+ thermalized; CO+continuum optically thick
- 2020ApJ...900....1F: Sersic index n=1
- 2018MNRAS.475.4924K: CO co-located with dust; stellar mass 2.18 Msun
- 2019A&A...632L...7J: flat continuum despite 1-2% change over sideband
- 2017ApJ...840...60B: dust opacity 2.9 cm2/g; abundances from Qi et al. 2011
- 2020ApJ...895..109F: T_mid0 fixed from literature (DM Tau 19 K freeze-out at 70 au; MWC 480 18.8 K; V4046 Sgr 12 K); distances from Gaia DR2
