### Limitations the authors admit
- 2018ApJ...852..122H: Models are not optimal; dust modeling and multi-line fitting deferred; perturbed temperature model not physically self-consistent
- 2018ApJ...852..122H: Absolute alpha uncertain by ~0.4 from flux calibration
- 2019MNRAS.484.4239R: Upper limits underestimated if CO is resolved; R21 and XCO uncertain
- 2019MNRAS.484.4239R: Projection effects limit alignment analysis; 3D modelling needed
- 2018A&A...615A.141B: Dust optically thick so N_H2 and mass are lower limits
- 2018A&A...615A.141B: Interferometer filters out extended emission
- 2018PASJ...70...36I: Mdyn has large unconstrained systematic uncertainty; sources only marginally resolved
- 2018A&A...615A..28D: Dust masses and dust-to-gas ratios uncertain by about a factor of 5
- 2018A&A...615A..28D: Extended emission may be resolved out
- 2020A&A...636A..67A: H2CO opacity may cause the differences in distribution and kinematics
- 2024ApJ...972..111L: Only projected distances and radial velocities known; spatial offset of redshifted [C II] smaller than beam
- 2024ApJ...966...59S: Short snapshot observations, lack of short spacings, gas radii as lower limits
- 2024ApJ...966...59S: Dust masses are lower limits if optically thick
- 2020ApJ...905...85S: Limited ALMA bandwidth prevents detection of redshifted P Cygni emission and caps vmax
- 2020ApJ...905...85S: Conservative classification is S/N dependent and may exclude weak outflows
- 2021A&A...648A..19W: Posterior uncertainties are small and likely underestimated; systematic model uncertainties
- 2021A&A...648A..19W: Pitch angles are only rough estimates from by-eye spiral parameterization
- 2024ApJ...961..228S: Protostellar mass is uncertain because Keplerian motion cannot be separated from the jet
- 2024ApJ...961..228S: Outflow mass and velocity are likely underestimated; field of view limits outflow length
- 2021A&A...656A..46M: Calibration uncertainty not included in fit uncertainties; line flux scaling anomalies in some tunings
- 2021A&A...656A..46M: STATCONT continuum subtraction not optimal for lines near noise level
- 2019A&A...628A.118B: Gas masses depend strongly on alpha_CO; large uncertainties on tau_dep and tau_SF
- 2015ApJ...814...22E: Simple spherical models do not perfectly match; abundance profiles are ad hoc
- 2014ApJ...797...90S: Mass estimates depend on uncertain X_CO; may be an order of magnitude lower if optically thin
- 2013ApJ...770...13W: Source only marginally resolved; intrinsic size poorly constrained and inclination unknown
- 2013ApJ...770...13W: L_FIR uncertainties exclude dust temperature uncertainty
- 2024MNRAS.527.9343L: Fluxes and masses for NGC 1194 and NGC 3393 are lower limits due to FoV; uncertainties exclude systematics
- 2024MNRAS.527.9343L: Spectral indices may be biased since resolution not matched to VLA
- 2019ApJ...882..118X: Uncertainties may be underestimated since continuum subtraction systematics not included
- 2012ApJ...757..129R: Model parameters are not unique nor optimized; limited resolution
- 2016ApJ...829....6W: CO mass assumes optically thin LTE and could be larger by a factor of a few or more
- 2016ApJ...829....6W: Debris mass depends strongly on assumed size distribution, density, albedo
- 2026ApJ..1002L..28Y: T_dust and beta assumed; multi-band FIR needed
- 2026ApJ..1002L..28Y: Pair fraction is a lower limit because the survey is incomplete
- 2019Natur.570...83M: Line could be unlucky combination of molecular lines or foreground absorption
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Common T_dust adopted for all sources; mass estimates depend on assumed conversion factors
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Spectral index maps only possible for 3 sources
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Small-number statistics for orientation and correlations
- 2019MNRAS.485..229R: Mass may differ by up to an order of magnitude due to X-factor and F_ul uncertainty
- 2019MNRAS.485..229R: Filling factor of 1 gives lower limit on tau; velocities are only apparent line-of-sight motions
- 2017Icar..286..289L: Lower mesosphere and stratopause temperatures are more uncertain, and the HCN vertical distribution is not unique given moderate optical thickness
- 2017Icar..286..289L: Spatial resolution insufficient to resolve surface
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Temperature poorly constrained by the data
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Calibration uncertainty not included in MCMC fit
- 2014A&A...570L..14R: Only ~50% of extended flux recovered even with ACA; dynamic range limited to ~50
- 2020A&A...644A..59K: Errors underestimated; isothermal assumption fails in center; SO2 fits unsatisfactory
- 2020A&A...644A..59K: Beam filling factors set to 1; no collisions with e- and H
- 2020A&A...644A..84M: Tex-Ntot degeneracy for AA gives a factor ~2 uncertainty on Ntot
- 2020A&A...644A..84M: Some MF transitions under-reproduced; unidentified blends possible
- 2024ApJ...968L..19F: Collisional rate coefficients for PH3-H2 unavailable; extended continuum emission resolved out may explain lower N(H2)
- 2024A&A...689A.317G: In-falling component size is not conclusive
- 2018MNRAS.481.4931E: Velocity resolution is modest and dynamical modelling is deferred.
- 2025A&A...693A.151M: Sample biased by flux-density limits; heights may be extracted from azimuthal profile rather than resolved
- 2020ApJ...890..167T: A single source of ~1e4 Msun cannot explain T2 and T3 kinematics; diffuse mass distribution possible
- 2025NatAs...9.1476C: HDO and H2O observed ~2 weeks apart; Q(H2O) inferred via CH3OH proxy
- 2025NatAs...9.1476C: Low S/N of HDO leaves L_p unconstrained for 50% distributed case
- 2014Sci...345.1584B: Preliminary LTE model not fully optimized for ALMA; abundance uncertainties exclude free-free contamination and dust property uncertainties
- 2013ApJ...777L..25M: Details of grain migration cannot be constrained by the data
- 2021A&A...647L...8C: Northern oval poorly viewed; northern detection tentative
- 2014ApJ...790..160S: Outflow quantities order-of-magnitude; XCO and line ratio uncertain
- 2014A&A...563A.136M: Mosaic fits require components small relative to the primary beam; no line-profile kinematics in the models
- 2014ApJ...791...95A: Departure from spherical symmetry would make the solution degenerate; finer resolution needed
- 2014ApJ...791...95A: Wind parameters during eruption cannot be strictly constrained
- 2017A&A...604A.115V: Flux measurements of 1b+3b are highly uncertain because of source shape
- 2024ApJ...963....1O: X_CO uncertainty may overestimate molecular mass by a factor of a few
- 2024ApJ...963....1O: Chandra data too shallow to resolve cavity
- 2015ApJ...808...97Y: SFR is only an order of magnitude estimate
- 2014ApJ...795L..30C: Single line per species insufficient to constrain the true HNC distribution
- 2014ApJ...784...78R: Cannot tell whether gas lies in front of or behind the BCG
- 2019ApJ...871..107F: Model does not fully reproduce observations because of 2D temperature structure uncertainties
- 2019ApJ...871..107F: Insufficient sensitivity to see the co-rotation bump
- 2018ApJ...863..143C: Some extended [CI] emission resolved out; flux 34±15% lower than Herschel
- 2018ApJ...863..143C: Outflow environment unprecedented; [CI]-based assumptions (X_CI, same gas as CO) uncertain
- 2018ApJ...866...87B: CS line emission not modelled because Band 10 data scales do not match
- 2018MNRAS.479.3879W: Spatial resolution ~1 arcsec insensitive to late-stage mergers, minor mergers and gas-poor companions
- 2018MNRAS.479.3879W: Targeted fields more sensitive to line-of-sight than sky-plane structure; small sample
- 2018A&A...614A..58B: Inner disk and width poorly constrained; mass depends on CO abundance and distance; LTE assumption; temperature uncertain
- 2020ApJ...898...10T: Model CBD larger than observed; magnetic field not included; high-velocity blueshifted components near Source N not reproduced; infall not identified observationally
- 2026A&A...705A..81K: Low per-channel S/N prevents full delensed cubes; source plane resolution insufficient to resolve clumps; results preliminary.
- 2024AJ....167...66Y: Emission only marginally resolved; midplane assumption; CH2DOH spectroscopy uncertain by ~factor 3
- 2020A&A...637A..84P: Poor angular resolution prevents constraining Mdyn for most; thin-disc assumption too simple for some perturbed systems; MBH systematics up to ~0.4 dex
- 2020ApJ...893..101L: Flux ratios are only a rough abundance proxy; high-Eu lines biased by temperature
- 2025ApJ...992..103Z: G14 RO distribution cannot be distinguished from random due to small numbers; G28 and I18360 excluded
- 2020ApJ...890...29F: Flux filtered by the interferometer on large scales is hard to quantify
- 2020ApJ...890...29F: N(H2) is a lower limit due to beam dilution and depends on alpha_CO
- 2019A&A...630A..59B: Interferometric data may miss extended diffuse emission; stacking dilutes orientations
- 2012A&A...548A..69N: Vibrationally excited emission unresolved at ~1.7"x1.2"; maser nature needs confirmation
- 2015ApJ...806...17R: Warm-gas mass per nucleus uses global Herschel ratio
- 2012ApJ...752L..30W: Lack of Tsys and WVR in the data adds 15% flux uncertainty; SW redshift unknown; outflow needs higher resolution
- 2025MNRAS.541.2540Z: Circular-orbit assumption with mild non-circular motions; distance uncertainty (10%) not included in budget
- 2019ApJ...871..112X: AcA morphology cannot be accurately determined due to few transitions and spatial contamination
- 2019ApJ...871..112X: Spectral simulation parameters chosen subjectively
- 2015ApJ...810..112O: Model is not tuned to IM Lup, so no quantitative comparison is possible
- 2015ApJ...810..112O: Outer-ring intensity is model dependent and may vary from disk to disk
- 2017MNRAS.465.2595M: Missing short baselines; no ACA; CO detection tentative and morphology inconsistent with simple Keplerian ring
- 2024PASJ...76..340K: Red component decomposition not unique; drift versus growth ambiguous; first epoch had poorer uv coverage
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: Distance mismatch between GRS 1915+105 and IRAS source; jet power assumes constant power and density
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: ALMA continuum lacks single-dish data so flux is underestimated
- 2020ApJ...892L..18I: Core component interpretation not conclusive.
- 2018ApJ...865...13T: X_CO uncertainty may overestimate mass by a factor of a few
- 2018ApJ...865...13T: Projection effects: motions in plane of sky unknown
- 2019AJ....158...76C: Limb retrievals are approximate due to coarse resolution and simplified polygonal parameterization
- 2019AJ....158...76C: Lifetime derivation relies on gross assumptions
- 2020MNRAS.497.2811K: Dust masses have large systematic uncertainties from arbitrary composition; HD 129590 gas unconstrained by MCMC
- 2015ApJ...814..143A: Smooth spherical shell model does not reproduce fine structure; infrared pumping only partly included
- 2020MNRAS.498L..87B: Emission unresolved; cannot distinguish envelope from disk; S hot corino needs higher resolution
- 2024ESC.....8..665M: Coarse resolution; morphology cannot be determined
- 2024A&A...686A.274V: Spatial filtering resolves out much CO flux, overestimating polarisation fractions by factor 2-3.
- 2024A&A...686A.274V: Circular polarisation of extended lines dominated by beam effects; no test of anisotropic resonant scattering.
- 2017MNRAS.464L..75F: Bipolar outflow versus rotating disc origin of H41alpha cannot be distinguished; filaments need more sensitive follow-up
- 2025A&A...698A.183D: ALMA resolution limits conclusions on the mm belt morphology
- 2020ApJ...894L..14L: Dust temperature at 2000 AU unknown, strongly affects masses
- 2020ApJ...894L..14L: Cannot tell whether cores are prestellar or protostellar
- 2024PSJ.....5..125T: Low S/N of CH3D prevents vertical profile; CH4 inference relies on prior D/H; beam smooths latitudinal structure
- 2015ApJ...803...97S: Many lines blended; Hot Core v_t=2 T_rot not determinable
- 2013ApJ...776...77K: Inner radius only an upper limit; brightness exponent ill-determined; full radiative transfer model postponed
- 2020ApJ...890...95I: Data quality limits accuracy; cannot distinguish UV vs GCR scenarios
- 2016ApJ...820L..25Y: Column density biased by poorly constrained dust and gas temperature profiles.
- 2017MNRAS.472.1239B: Lack of H30alpha from fainter sources could bias SFR downward; most continuum emission <5 sigma
- 2017A&A...604A...6S: Interferometer resolves out emission above ~5'', affecting faint-source spectral indices

